## Unhandled feedback submission failure allows false success message

**What fails\:** The feedback component in `docs/components/geistdocs/feedback.tsx` ignores the success status returned by `sendFeedback()`\, causing the \"Thank you for your feedback\!\" message to display even when the feedback submission fails\.

**How to reproduce\:**

1.  Open the feedback popover on any documentation page
2.  Network request to `/feedback` endpoint fails \(network error\, server error\, etc\.\)
3.  The feedback form dismisses and shows \"Thank you for your feedback\!\" despite the request failing
4.  User believes feedback was submitted when it was not

**Result\:** Failed feedback submissions appear successful to the user\, leading to poor UX and data loss

**Expected behavior\:** Per [sonner toast documentation](https://sonner.emilkowal.ski/)\, failed submissions should show an error toast\, and successful submissions should show the success message\. The `sendFeedback()` server action returns `{ success: boolean }` to indicate outcome\, which must be checked before updating UI state\.

**Fix\:** Check the `success` property from `sendFeedback()` before setting `submitted` to true\. On failure\, display an error toast using the imported `sonner` library \(already used elsewhere in the codebase per code\-block\.tsx\)\. Also added try\-catch to handle any potential errors from the server action\.

